Built stdlib-only compress.py with both requested CLI modes, learned record templates and numeric patterns, compact symbol encoding, and a bzip2 fallback. All reconstruction metadata is stored in the compressed file. The 313,972-byte corpus compresses to 2,939 bytes (99.0639% reduction), beating default zlib’s 35,399 bytes. Verified byte-identical round trips, randomized fallback tests, and independent decompression without corpus.txt present. Registered python3 assay.py; three runs returned identical fitness.